{"rubric_version":"opencode-browser-856867996e73f7dcc5e39827bf2af7555bd63d40-judge-prompt.md","attempt":1,"prompt":[{"role":"system","content":"# WebVoyager Benchmark Evaluation\n\nYou are an evaluator for a web browsing agent benchmark. You will receive:\n\n1. **WebVoyager_data.json** — the task definitions (task_id, confirmed_task, website)\n2. **results.ndjson** — the agent's execution results (one JSON per line)\n\n## Your Job\n\nFor each result in results.ndjson, judge whether the agent successfully completed the task.\n\n## Evaluation Rules\n\n**PASS** if:\n- The agent's `final_answer` contains the specific information requested by the task\n- The information is factually plausible (e.g., a recipe with \"4.5 stars\" when task asks for \"at least 4.5 stars\")\n- Minor formatting differences, extra information, or verbose answers are acceptable\n- Partial completion counts as PASS only if the core requirement is met\n\n**FAIL** if:\n- `status` is \"error\" or \"timeout\" AND `final_answer` is empty or does not answer the task\n- The answer is wrong, irrelevant, or hallucinatory\n- The answer is generic (e.g., \"I found a recipe\" without providing the actual recipe details)\n- The agent failed to find the requested information and said so\n- Key requirements are missing (e.g., task asks for \"rating above 4.5\" but agent's answer shows a 3-star recipe)\n\n**NOTE**: If `status` is \"error\" but `final_answer` still contains a valid answer to the task, judge it as PASS.\n\n## Output Format\n\nReturn a JSON array, one object per task:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"task_id\": \"Allrecipes--0\",\n    \"pass\": true,\n    \"reason\": \"Agent found a vegetarian lasagna recipe with 4.6 stars and 150+ reviews, matching all criteria.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"task_id\": \"Allrecipes--1\",\n    \"pass\": false,\n    \"reason\": \"Agent returned a lasagna recipe but it does not use zucchini as required.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nRequirements for each entry:\n- `task_id`: must match exactly\n- `pass`: boolean\n- `reason`: one sentence explaining why pass or fail, referencing the specific task requirement\n\n## Important\n\n- Compare `final_answer` against `confirmed_task` from WebVoyager_data.json for each matching `task_id`\n- Do NOT skip any result — every entry in results.ndjson must have a judgment\n- Be strict on whether the core task requirement is met, but lenient on presentation\n- If the task asks for multiple things (e.g., \"find a recipe AND list ingredients\"), all parts must be present to PASS\n\nEvaluate all results now.\n"},{"role":"user","content":"WebVoyager_data.json\n[{\"task_id\":\"ESPN--6\",\"confirmed_task\":\"Find the result of the latest basketball game between the Los Angeles Lakers and the Boston Celtics, including the final score and top scorer from the match.\",\"website\":\"https://www.espn.com/\"}]\n\nresults.ndjson\n{\"task_id\":\"ESPN--6\",\"website\":\"https://www.espn.com/\",\"task\":\"Find the result of the latest basketball game between the Los Angeles Lakers and the Boston Celtics, including the final score and top scorer from the match.\",\"session_id\":\"eval-ESPN--6-a43653dcf4fe\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"duration_ms\":445585,\"steps\":39,\"tokens\":{\"input\":198626,\"output\":11285,\"cache_read\":364088,\"cache_write\":0,\"reasoning\":8737},\"cost\":0.09497508,\"final_answer\":\"I have all the information needed to provide the answer. Let me provide the final response.\\n\\n## Final Answer\\n\\n**The latest basketball game between the Los Angeles Lakers and Boston Celtics:**\\n\\n📅 **Date:** February 23, 2026 (NBA regular season)\\n\\n🏀 **Final Score:**\\n- **Boston Celtics: 111**\\n- **Los Angeles Lakers: 89**\\n\\nThe Celtics won the game, completing a **season series sweep (2-0)** of the Lakers. The Lakers had also lost to the Celtics earlier in the season on December 6, 2025 (126-105).\\n\\n🌟 **Top Scorer from the Match:**\\n- **Jaylen Brown** (Boston Celtics) — **32 points** (10/28 FG, 9/12 FT), along with 8 rebounds and 7 assists\\n\\n**Other notable performances:**\\n- **Luka Doncic** (Lakers) — 25 points (9/22 FG, 3/6 FT)\\n- **Neemias Queta** (Celtics) — 12 rebounds (8 defensive, 4 offensive)\\n- **Payton Pritchard** (Celtics) — 8 assists\\n- **LeBron James** (Lakers) — 5 assists\\n- **Austin Reaves** (Lakers) — 7 rebounds\\n\\nThe Celtics dominated the game, leading in field goal percentage (48% vs 39%) and three-point percentage (39% vs 30%), with 50 rebounds to the Lakers' 39.\\n\\n**Note:** The Celtics and Lakers did not meet in the 2025-26 NBA playoffs. The Celtics were eliminated in the first round by Philadelphia (3-4), while the Lakers made it to the second round before being swept by Oklahoma City (0-4).\",\"tool_trace\":[{\"tool\":\"browser_start\",\"input\":{\"url\":\"https://www.espn.com/\"},\"call_id\":\"call_01a0dc88da3b72f6a2a69b7c\",\"time_ms\":17592,\"output_preview\":\"# Browser Mode\\n\\nThe DSH browser plugin controls a real Chromium instance isolated to the current Agent Session.\\n\\n- DOM markers `[N]` are clickable and `<N>` are inputs.\\n- Match element labels or nearby text, and use DOM indentation to distinguish parents, children, and siblings; do not choose by mar\",\"status\":\"success\"},{\"tool\":\"browser_click\",\"input\":{\"elementIndex\":7432,\"expectText\":\"NBA\"},\"call_id\":\"call_01a0dc89244a700a8289e4b9\",\"time_ms\":13115,\"output_preview\":\"Clicked <a> NBA </a> Postcondition verified.\\n\\n\\n<!-- DOM_START dom0.1 tab:tab0 mode:full -->\\n(stateId: tab0-dom0.1)\\n## Current Page DOM Structure\\n\\n\\n<section></section>\\n\\t<div></div>\\n\\t\\t[361]<button aria-label='Select league' type='button'> NBA </button>\\n\\t<div></div>\\n\\t\\t[489]<button type='button'> Oct 3 \",\"status\":\"success\"},{\"tool\":\"browser_goto\",\"input\":{\"url\":\"https://www.espn.com/nba/scoreboard\"},\"call_id\":\"call_01a0dc89623573989f76caa6\",\"time_ms\":8017,\"output_preview\":\"Navigated to https://www.espn.com/nba/scoreboard\\n\\n\